{red|**Take time to honestly explore your spiritual state.**

How has divorce affected your relationship with God?}{red| What questions or doubts have emerged?}{red| What spiritual practices have you abandoned or maintained?}{red| What do you need from God right now?}

Write about your spiritual struggles:

{red|**Explore what you have believed about God's love since your divorce.**

Have you felt that God loves you less?}{red| Have you felt disqualified from His blessing?}{red| What messages have contributed to these beliefs?}{red| What would change if you truly believed His love is unchanged?}

Write about what you have believed:

{red|What honest feelings toward God have you been hiding?}

{red|Are you angry at Him?}{red| About what specifically?}{red| Are you disappointed?}{red| What did you expect that did not happen?}{red| Are you confused?}{red| What questions do you have?}{red| Are you hurt?}{red| How?}

Write your honest feelings toward God:

{red|What hard questions about faith and divorce are you wrestling with?}

{red|What questions about God trouble you?}{red| What questions about the Bible and divorce concern you?}{red| What do you fear might be true?}{red| What do you hope is true?}

Write your hard questions:

{red|**Reflect on your experience with church since your divorce.**

How has church felt since your divorce?}{red| Do you feel welcomed and supported, or judged and marginalized?}{red| What do you need from a church community that you are not currently getting?}{red| What would help you engage with church more fully?}

Write about your church experience:

{red|**Create a plan for engaging with church community.**

If you are staying at your current church, what steps will you take to engage more fully or address challenges?}

{red|If you are looking for a new church, what will you look for and how will you search?}

{red|If you have stepped back, what would help you re-engage?}

{red|Are there divorce recovery groups or other specific communities you could join?}

Write your church engagement plan:

{red|**Assess your current support network.**

Who do you have who truly knows and supports you?}{red| What types of support are you getting?}{red| What is missing?}{red| Where could you find the community you need?}{red| What barriers keep you from connecting with others?}

Write your support assessment:

{red|**Reflect on your current spiritual practices.**

What spiritual practices have you maintained through your divorce?}{red| What practices have fallen away?}{red| What feels accessible to you right now?}{red| What feels too hard?}{red| What do you need from spiritual practices in this season?}

Write about your spiritual practices:

{red|**Reflect on your sense of purpose since your divorce.**

Have you felt disqualified from God's purposes?}{red| What ministry or contribution opportunities have you lost or stepped back from?}{red| What might God still want to do through you?}{red| How might your painful experience actually prepare you for something?}

Write about your sense of purpose:

{red|**Identify where you most need grace right now.**

What feels too hard without God's help?}{red| Where are you being too hard on yourself?}{red| What fears about the future require grace?}{red| Where do you need to receive what God is offering?}

Write about where you need grace:

{red|What is the most important thing you have learned or received through this journey about faith and community after divorce?}

{red|What do you want to remember when you struggle spiritually?}

Write your key insight:

{red|What commitments will you make for your ongoing spiritual health?}

{red|How will you nurture your relationship with God?}{red| How will you engage with church or Christian community?}{red| How will you handle spiritual struggles when they arise?}{red| How will you extend grace to yourself?}

